.TH PHYLLO-STATUS 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo-status \- inspect resolved project integration state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo status
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --no-color ]
.br
.B phyllo status --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo status
reports the invoked phyllo CLI version, discovered project root, adapter,
configuration source, selected semantic profile, installed Phyllotaxis package
version/path, and installed/configured Venation contract values.
Status is an inspection command: success does not establish contract validity.
It does not modify the project or execute project-provided scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select human-readable text or the versioned JSON result. Text is the default.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-error human success and informational output. It does not suppress
errors, alter machine output, or change the exit status.
.TP
.B --no-color
Disable ANSI color in human output. This is also implied by non-TTY output, NO_COLOR, or TERM=dumb.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help without discovering a project.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Project and package metadata were inspected successfully.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, or required package resolution error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational error prevented inspection.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo (1),
.BR phyllo-check (1),
.BR phyllo-doctor (1)
